anked 5th of 8 - the purest H-acid exposure in the cluster and the ONLY name with a second, independent lever: it is itself the applicant in a live DGTR anti-dumping investigation into Beta Naphthol from China. Trades at 1.07x book, barely above the value of eight plants in a business where global capacity is the binding constraint. What holds it back: its Dye Intermediates segment actually FELL 4% in Q1 while margin compressed 11.66% -> 9.72%, and it carries ESM Stage I - a 100% margin requirement, so effectively no MTF. Q2 FY27 (around November) is the decisive test: it is the first quarter that contains the H-acid move at all.","rank":34},{"code":"IGPL","name":"I G Petrochems","sector":"Chemicals & Petrochemicals","industry":"Commodity Chemicals","band":"Micro","mcap":1814,"price":588.95,"score":11.0,"rs":82,"sector_rs":64,"r1d":4.53,"r1w":6.2,"from_52wh":-0.91,"new_high":true,"trend":"7/7","trend_pass":true,"s2":{"weeks":7.0,"status":"Continues Trend","rs_pct":19.05,"since":"2026-08-01"},"reasons":["at a new 52-week high","on the Stage 2 list (7 wks)","still early in the Stage 2 move","passes the trend template (7/7)","up 4.5% today","RS 82","Chemicals & Petrochemicals is a leading sector"],"pinned":true,"pin_note":"Ranked 4th of 8, just 0.2 behind Foseco - effectively tied for third, and the comparative note says to read it as a co-equal third if the preference runs to cheapness over quality. A Rs 8.2 Cr loss became a Rs 71 Cr profit with the margin swinging 1,778bps, the largest single-year move in the library. ~5.8x annualised earnings, 1.22x book. The risk is that it is a pure spread business with no control over either end. Watching the PAN-orthoxylene spread and the plasticizer plant starting commercial production in September 2026.","rank":52},{"code":"BHAGERIA","name":"Bhageria Indust.","sector":"Chemicals & Petrochemicals","industry":"Dyes And Pigments","band":"Micro","mcap":1535,"price":351.75,"score":8.0,"rs":94,"sector_rs":64,"r1d":1.88,"r1w":10.32,"