owth holds in the mid-teens (the +78% profit was operating leverage in a good quarter, not a run-rate) and whether it holds up once the chemicals rotation fades.","rank":259},{"code":"GIPCL","name":"Guj Inds. Power","sector":"Power","industry":"Power Generation","band":"Micro","mcap":2975,"price":191.64,"score":4.0,"rs":65,"sector_rs":32,"r1d":2.53,"r1w":2.97,"from_52wh":-9.48,"new_high":false,"trend":"6/7","trend_pass":false,"s2":{"weeks":5.0,"status":"Continues Trend","rs_pct":20.38,"since":"2026-08-15"},"reasons":["on the Stage 2 list (5 wks)","still early in the Stage 2 move","up 2.5% today"],"pinned":true,"pin_note":"Ranked 1st of 8 in the chemicals-cluster comparative note. Cheapest name there at 6.3x earnings and 0.83x book, with a 48.4% operating margin that is structural (Khavda solar, near-zero marginal cost) rather than cyclical. Watching the Rs 7,000 Cr lignite decision and the Q3 FY27 500 MW commissioning.","rank":444}]}